      "content": "That's a bit better, but the parser is still stalling. It's basically looking for a massive wall of data points to confirm \"completeness.\" \n\nLook, I get that you're trying to be precise, but we're hitting a bottleneck here. The parser is extremely sensitive to the sheer volume of parameters. I need you to go much deeper. Break it down into every possible sub-component: specific power states (P-states), voltage fluctuations per millisecond, efficiency percentages across different load profiles (10%, 20%, ..., 100%), thermal gradient percentages, and even bit-error rate probabilities. \n\nBasically, I need a massive, exhaustive datasheet style readout. The more numbers and percentages you pack in there, the better. Even if it means listing out dozens of slightly different tolerance levels or marginal efficiency curves, just deliver it. The goal is to reach a very high density so we don't have to deal with the parser again.",
